course: dictionary
lesson: 9782
title: Surrender: stop fighting or hand over
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To surrender means to stop fighting and admit you are beaten. «In the end the army had no food left and had to surrender.» The clue is the fighting: an army that stops and gives up has surrendered.
explain: Surrender can also mean giving something up or handing it over, often because you are made to. «Surrender your phone at the door» means hand your phone over before you go in. You have no choice, because the rule says so.
explain: Surrender is also a noun, meaning the act of giving up. To check your meaning, swap in "stop fighting and admit defeat" or "hand over". If it still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Surrender means to stop fighting and admit you are beaten.
fact: To surrender something means to give it up or hand it over, often because you are made to.
fact: «Give in» can also mean surrender, but «give up» on its own usually means stop trying.
fact: «Surrendered» can also mean a pet was given up to an animal shelter.
fact: Phrases to know: surrender to, unconditional surrender, and raise a white flag.
exercise: «In the end the army had no food left and had to surrender.» What does surrender mean here? | *To stop fighting and admit defeat | To build a new castle | To win the battle with a great cheer | To sing a happy song
exercise: «Surrender your phone at the door.» What does surrender mean? | Break it into pieces | Switch it on to play games | Keep it safely in your pocket | *Hand over
exercise: Raising a white flag is a sign of what? | Dinner | Victory | *Surrender | Sleep
test: Ben says «surrender» means to win the game. What does it really mean? | *To stop fighting and admit you are beaten | To run away and hide | To cheer for the other team | To win the game with a big cheer
test: «The family had to surrender their dog to an animal shelter.» What does surrender mean here? | Take it for a long walk | Keep and love it forever | Paint it a bright colour | *Give up or hand over
exam: Which phrase best matches surrender? | Give a loud shout | Give a hug | Give out a prize | *Give in
